Package: BriDGE
Type: Package
Title: Behavioural Research by Integrating DAGs and GAMs in Experiments
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Giuseppe", "Veltri",
      email = "gaveltri@nus.edu.sg",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9472-2236")
    )
  )
Description: Implements the BriDGE protocol for mechanistic causal analysis of
    randomized controlled trial (RCT) data, as described in Veltri and Banerjee
    (in press, Behavior Research Methods), "BriDGE the gap - improving
    Behavioural research by integrating DAGs and GAMs in Experiments". BriDGE
    combines causal discovery with experimental constraints (structure learning
    via 'bnlearn' with treatment-edge whitelists and blacklists), mediation
    analysis with nonlinear relationships through Generalized Additive Models
    (GAMs, via 'mgcv'), bootstrap-based uncertainty quantification, sensitivity
    analysis, and visualization. The package is agnostic to specific data
    structures, making it suitable for researchers across domains who need to
    move from "what works" to "why and how it works" in experimental data.
    Key features include support for multiple mediators, parallel processing,
    and integrated diagnostic tools for model validation.
